# Explore temporary sessions for incognito use

Consider an incognito mode whose session lives in temporary storage and is cleaned up when its owner exits.

Suggestions:
- Clarify the privacy promise, including what remains outside the transcript such as provider requests or tool-created files.
- Inspect explicit session paths and scratch cleanup before adding a separate session lifecycle.
- Explore ownership when background turns, subagents, handoffs, or cancellation outlive the client.
- Keep the ordinary append-only transcript as the session state even when its storage is temporary.

